One file per Erdős problem, named for its number: `Erdos/359.lean`, module
`Erdos.«359»` (a numeric component is not a legal Lean identifier, so an
import has to write the French quotes: `import Erdos.«359»`).

This placeholder is not decoration. The `Erdos` library target in
`../lakefile.toml` uses the glob `Erdos.+`, and Lake resolves that by walking
the `Erdos/` directory; if the directory does not exist, `lake build Erdos`
fails with "no such file or directory" rather than building nothing. Git does
not track empty directories, so without this file a fresh clone has no
`Erdos/` at all. Delete it only once real problem files live here.
